+# Kart driver anatomy and pedal contact — 2026-11-08
+
+The owner rejects the feet missing the pedals and the appearance of the arms, legs and torso, explicitly asking for AAA quality. This revision fixes the measurable control fit and reconstructs the garment. **It does not establish AAA art quality or owner appearance acceptance.** The selected source is a very coarse, unrigged static character; the remaining helmet/glove/boot geometry and limited clothing detail remain visible limitations. Earlier fit/style test passes did not prove pedal contact or acceptable anatomy.
+
+| Requirement | Implemented change and evidence |
+| --- | --- |
+| KDA01 — feet on the pedals | Rotate the boots 72.811° from the standing sole orientation. Flatten the original tread vertices and fit the load-bearing sole patch to the existing PedalPlate face with 1 mm clearance. Native tests locate both actual pedal meshes and ray-test nine distributed samples on each plate, in both quality tiers. They also check parallel sole triangles, penetration and heel height. The rejected mesh is retained as a failing control. |
+| KDA02 — arms, legs and torso | Solve knees and elbows with two-bone targets, rather than choosing unrelated joint positions. Target thigh/shin lengths are 0.445/0.440 model metres; knee flexion is 57.608°. Torso recline is 35° with an upright helmet. Round the source torso cross-sections and narrow the forearms toward the cuffs. Preserve the already enlarged 0.42 anatomy scale and helmet width. |
+| KDA03 — continuous clothing | Subdivide the source garment before deformation, weld source positional seams, reconstruct the occupied volume of its capped sections, smooth their junctions, and remesh the union. Simplify that dense authoring intermediate offline with the engine's existing ImporterMesh operation and recompute the retained surface normals. Native slate panels, dark cuffs/waist and a surface-fitted centre seam provide garment definition without photographic fabric or lettering. No new raster generation, dependency, skeleton or runtime posing is introduced. |
+| KDA04 — integrated appearance | Bake the native resource and body shadow; rebuild prepared bases, fitted modules and Garage templates; refresh the catalogue, news, header, livery and Garage pictures. Verify actual prepared hits and actual App Garage/race views. Concurrent Super Rally/scenery changes remain preserved. |
+
+The native driver has **7,319 triangles / seven materials**: 5,918 continuous-suit triangles, a 544-triangle fitted centre seam, and 857 retained helmet/face/glove/boot triangles. The approximately 379,000-triangle volume reconstruction is an offline intermediate and is not shipped. This deliberately supersedes the rejected version's 1,343-triangle/source-topology assertions; increasing triangle count alone is not an art-quality claim. A lower-pelvis corrective aligns the actual hip reference to the limb targets while preserving head/chest height; the final lower pelvic envelope is 0.2532, about 4.2?4.3 mm above the sampled padded pan minimum. Source helmet UVs and the previously reviewed unbranded helmet image remain. CC BY 4.0 attribution by tomkart remains in Settings → Licences.
+
+Native review: [side](evidence/kart-driver-anatomy-2026-11-08/candidate-side-right.png), [body close-up](evidence/kart-driver-anatomy-2026-11-08/candidate-body.png), [pedal close-up](evidence/kart-driver-anatomy-2026-11-08/candidate-feet.png), [front](evidence/kart-driver-anatomy-2026-11-08/candidate-front.png). These are actual Godot renders of the replacement in the existing kart, with its original controls and seat.
+
+## Reproduction and scope
+
+The selected owner-supplied ZIP remains under `docs/evidence/kart-tomkart-driver-2026-11-08/source/`. `scripts/prepare_kart_driver.py` and the new numpy-only `scripts/kart_driver_geometry.py` author the static candidate. `game/tests/bake_tomkart_driver.gd` bakes its native materials and mesh. `test_kart_driver_contact.gd` supplies the new actual-surface regression; `test_tomkart_driver.gd` retains size, finite normals, material, articulation, paint-isolation and prepared-restoration checks for the revised geometry. Runtime pose/seat/controls/camera builders and canonical handling are unchanged by this task.
+
+```powershell
+python scripts/prepare_kart_driver.py docs/evidence/kart-tomkart-driver-2026-11-08/source/race_car_driver_-_low_poly.zip --output build/kart-driver-anatomy-2026-11-08/candidate
+python scripts/run_kart_driver_review.py candidate-bake res://tests/bake_tomkart_driver.gd --headless -- --preview
+python scripts/run_kart_driver_review.py candidate-contact res://tests/test_kart_driver_contact.gd --headless
+python scripts/run_kart_driver_review.py contact-before-control res://tests/test_kart_driver_contact.gd --headless -- --before
+python scripts/run_kart_driver_review.py final-preview res://tests/review_tomkart_driver.gd --rendering-method gl_compatibility
+python scripts/run_kart_driver_review.py shipping-driver-bake res://tests/bake_tomkart_driver.gd --headless
+python scripts/run_kart_driver_review.py shipping-direct res://tests/test_tomkart_driver.gd --headless
+python build/kart-driver-anatomy-2026-11-08/rebuild.py
+```
+
+Exact commands, engine version, exits and logs are retained in the evidence directory. The runner pins `4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf`, uses private offline APPDATA/LOCALAPPDATA and Dummy audio, and retains the known Windows certificate-store diagnostic. The normal dev wrapper treats that diagnostic as fatal. Native test windows are offscreen; no owner process is restarted. The runner records its own child PID and raises an explicit cleanup error when sandboxed termination is refused, instead of waiting indefinitely after a failed taskkill.
+
+## Validation and retained findings
+
+The native pedal/hand/floor/seat matrix passes **27/0**. Both feet cover all nine actual pedal samples at a maximum measured **1.0024 mm** gap in both tiers. The rejected mesh fails **14/27** checks (the earlier pedal-only control failed 12/21) and covers **zero** pedal samples. Gloves have multiple nearby steering-rim vertices; that proximity check is not an animation or grasp-quality claim. Direct geometry/material/integration checks pass **63/0**, including order-independent triangle comparisons against restored drivers (the earlier 59/0 run predates those four additional comparisons), and driving passes **72/0**. Final prepared/native/App results are recorded in `final-summary.json` beside this report's evidence.
+
+Initial failures remain available. The first new sole patch passed only seven of nine samples, with 4.252 mm maximum gap; correcting the tread plane resolves it without relaxing the 3 mm gate. The repeated right-hand pedal receives an automatic Godot node name; the test now identifies it through the same actual mesh resource as the first plate, rather than silently testing one foot. Early dense and unrefined renders are retained in `draft-1/`.
+
+PowerShell execution policy prevented the first identity invocation; the process-scoped standard Bypass invocation succeeds. A concurrent new `SuperRallyModel` reference was initially absent from Godot's class cache; a headless editor import refresh registers it, and subsequent kart bakes pass. Only the verified task-owned failed command tree was stopped. One wash invocation used a nonexistent filename; the real broad wash fixture then reaches its existing direct `HEIGHTS["super_rally"]` lookup and fails because that fixture assumes the earlier five-car catalogue. That failure and any narrower original-five-car controls are retained, without changing production weathering or weakening wash tolerances. The rebuild helper's initial header-template filename typo is retained if reached; the correct existing baker is `bake_header_simple_compact.gd`.
+
+Task-start source files, native driver and hashes are retained under `before/`. The source checkpoint records task-only before/after text and asset hashes; it does not stage or commit the shared index. Generated outputs remain subject to the existing source guards. No device query/test, APK, owner-save edit, owner-process restart, backend request or deployment is performed. Reload, owner appearance acceptance and device qualification remain. A higher-quality character asset and further art production are still required to meet the owner's AAA target.
+
+
+## Final live results and concurrent work
+
+Final live kart cache checks pass **70/0 headless** and **80/0 on each desktop renderer**. All four base modes and the Garage template actually restore, and their driver triangle geometry matches the reviewed mesh. Actual App Garage/race checks pass **16/0 on each renderer**, including current Garage geometry matching direct construction, screenshots at three window sizes, race identity and wheel articulation. The final Garage image audit passes **six exact images / 157 current source hashes**. The gallery helper restores unrelated PNGs from its immediate pre-bake copy; subsequent concurrent work rerendered those images and its current files are preserved. Four wheel shadows remain byte-exact to task start. Preservation comparisons and rerender controls remain separate. Runtime asset size is 1,435,427 bytes. The body shadow is 1,173 triangles; the wheel shadows retain their original geometry.
+
+The final pelvis corrective seats the source hip reference consistently with the leg targets. Its measured lower envelope is 0.2532, compared with pan minima 0.2489/0.2490. The initially rejected driver's same envelope was 0.1814. This additional correction and its six assertions were applied before final native/App acceptance; earlier 7,503-triangle drafts and their receipts remain in `pre-hip-correction/`.
+
+One earlier complete 520-module rebuild passed against its then-current sources. A later identity generation encountered a concurrent writer holding a Super Rally module. The existing PowerShell function continued after the read exception and wrote empty generated constants; only that known-invalid generated state and its empty project version were restored from the last valid receipt. Current shared metadata was subsequently refreshed by the concurrent work and is valid. The task helper now uses terminating PowerShell errors so that its identity stage stops before writing such a partial result. No shared build-script implementation or source guard was weakened.
+
+A stable project copy was prepared as a contingency; its Kart leaf builders match the live versions. No frozen generated binaries were copied back. Final live validation instead rebuilds only the kart's own four bases, 60 modules and Garage template against the refreshed shared metadata, then passes the native/App checks above. The shared preflight initially retains **16 stale-key failures in Electric simple modules** while that independent rebuild is in progress. After those files actually change, a fresh run passes **551 resources / 2,267 checks / zero failures**. The final six-image/157-source audit also passes. Both the initial failure and final clean receipts remain. This validates prepared dependencies at that point; no APK, export or device acceptance is claimed. Source-only patch forward/reverse verification and Python compilation are recorded with the checkpoint. Existing first-draw race hitches remain; no performance or hardware-memory gain is claimed.
